# Harness core v2

The harness's runtime, rebuilt in the shape of [HarnessPro](https://github.com/pzs19/HarnessPro)
(commit `6fd2d4d`, 2026-10-28): a short always-loaded contract, a `policy.json` with Lite,
Medium and Heavy profiles, and one standard-library hook. Everything else the harness knows lives
in modules that a prompt loads only when it needs them. Decision record: `docs/adr/0017-core-v2.md`.

| File | What it is |
|---|---|
| `instructions.md` | The contract. Installed as the always-loaded rule file of every agent (`~/.claude/rules/harness-runtime.md`, Codex/Copilot instructions; OMP gets it at session start). |
| `policy.json` | Profiles, the prompt classifier, heavy paths, guard prefilters, output limits and the module table. Tune behaviour here, not in code. |
| `hook.py` | The wired entry: loads `runtime.py` (bytecode-cached) and falls back to the last tested copy when it breaks (Entry and last-good copy below). Small and stable; replace it only by an atomic rename. |
| `runtime.py` | The one hook's logic. Standard library only; guard modules under `scripts/` are loaded by path only when a command or edit matches their prefilter. |
| `install.py` | `apply`, `status`, `env`. |
| `measure.py` | Median latency and injected bytes per event; `--score` rates the classifiers on a labelled set. |

## Events

| Event | Claude | Codex | Job |
|---|---|---|---|
| UserPromptSubmit | yes | yes | Guess the profile from the words of the prompt at once and start a background second opinion from the client's small model, name up to three modules plus those the session's project calls for (`context_modules`: a web project loads `web` on "ok, go" too, its `package.json` read once per session and directory), and on a session's first prompt add the marker `HARNESS_ACTIVE:core-v2:<hash>` and the user's learned preferences (`user-memory.md`, capped at 1,600 characters). Show the few items of the user's own apps the prompt is about (Recall below). A lite prompt after the first injects nothing else. URLs are not read as the user's words (a host like `x.harness-cards.pages.dev` made a question heavy). A client's one-shot helper prompt (Orca's "Name this chat ...", 63 a day) gets nothing and starts no model call; a relayed message (Stop hook feedback, another session's message) continues the task like a task notification. |
| PreToolUse | yes | yes | Safety rails, plus two Claude Agent checks: unsafe deletion targets (`scripts/permission_judge.py` `target_rail`), the shell guard (`scripts/shell_guard.py`), the money freeze (`scripts/money_policy.py`), unproven model-config edits (`scripts/model_preflight.py`), user-only files (`own-part.md`, `explorations.md`), one refusal of a whole-file read of a Markdown file over 40 KB, plan mode only when the user asked for a plan; for Claude's Agent tool, a refusal of Jobs review round 6 when the brief's `jobs-review.json` holds 5 rounds and the latest is not satisfied, and a note pointing a fresh verifier at the session's acceptor (resume it with SendMessage); for Claude's SendMessage to that acceptor asking for a verdict, a diff-only note at round 2 and a refusal of round 4 (7, 10, ...) until the request carries `Approach re-evaluated:` or the user asked for more rounds (review must converge: 29% of judged acceptors ran 3+ rounds, 2026-10-28; rounds per acceptor live in the session state, observed history in `review_ledger.py stats`); the first edit of a front-end file brings the `web` module once to a Claude session that has not had it (`context_modules`; harness and temp-folder pages excepted); and the move to heavy when an edit touches a heavy path or a command changes the machine or agent setup (`escalate_commands`). |
| PostToolUse | yes | yes | Apply the second opinion when it has arrived (it never lowers a profile an edit or command raised); count tool calls per prompt; remember the acceptors Claude spawns (id, description, prompt number); at the profile's economy and strict counts, tell the agent to economise or converge. After an edit, queue the checks the edited path maps to (Edit-time checks below) and report any that failed. Codex only: a shell output over the profile's limit is shortened to a head/tail view and kept in full under `<state>/core/raw/<session>/`. |
| PermissionRequest | yes | — | Claude stops for a command it finds dangerous; the independent reviewer (`permission_judge.verdict`) answers instead of the user. Fires only then, so it costs nothing on ordinary calls. A command the model could never allow (not every target a literal scratch path) is denied at once without the model call (22 decisions on 2026-10-29, …179 tokens truncated…
  `<state>/core/notices/`, apart from the session state). With no last-good copy the call fails open
  with that notice; a permission request is denied.
- Only tested bytes reach last-good: the `promote` row of `edit_checks` (core-v2) reads `runtime.py`
  and `policy.json` before `test_core_v2` and writes them after a pass only if they are unchanged
  (`LastGood` rows in `events.jsonl`). A session's first prompt starts the same test in the background,
  once per source version, when last-good does not hold the current source (a pull on another machine).
- Not covered: an error in `hook.py` itself (no fallback; `python-syntax` checks it at edit time) and the
  guard modules under `scripts/`, which load from the working tree and fail open one by one.
- A missing `hook.py` blocks every tool call (Python exits 2, a blocking hook error in Claude Code), so
  the file is replaced only by writing a temporary file and renaming it over the old one.

Loading the runtime as a module lets Python reuse its compiled bytecode instead of compiling the whole
file on every event: 5 to 7.5 ms less per event (paired runs below).

Adopted from HarnessPro on 2026-10-29:

