# Scene and pupil play-test findings

1. `/play/scene`, **True or false?**, round 5, both viewports: select session 2; correct rounds 1–4 (`in`, `right of`, `on`, `in front of`); in round 5 change the key's relation to `on`, then Check against the stage. The green check says “The key is on the book”, but the key stands diagonally in the air above the book rather than lying on its cover. Reproduced in a fresh context after waiting 2.5 seconds: `phone-scene-2-5-settled.png`, `desktop-scene-2-5-settled.png`. Fix the key-on-book sprite/anchor so its visible footprint rests on the book; don't use the standing key geometry for the on relation.
2. `/play/pupil`, **Teach the pupil**, round 3, both viewports: advance through a/an and plurals; in past-tense round read the second Explain option, then teach until all five answers pass. The rule says “double a final consonant only after a short, stressed vowel” while `preferred` is taught as correct. British `prefer` has long /ɜː/; this is a spelling pattern involving a single vowel letter and final stress, not this blanket vowel-length condition. Screenshots: `desktop-pupil-1-3-explanation.png`, `phone-pupil-1-3-judged.png`. Fix: describe single-vowel-letter + single-final-consonant spelling with final-syllable stress, excluding w/x/y, while retaining the British/American l note. References: https://dictionary.cambridge.org/pronunciation/english/prefer and https://our-languages.canada.ca/en/writing-tips-plus/spelling-final-consonants-doubled-before-a-suffix .
3. `/play/pupil`, **Rules with no rule**, round 1 twist, both viewports: teach with the swim example cards, then select Now a word it hasn't seen. The prompt says “Your example sentence said ‘He stopped smoking’”, although no stopped-smoking example was given (the deck has want/plan/mind/practise/promise/keep + swim). Choosing Correct it gives “Not this time” even though its own feedback acknowledges a different meaning from the alleged model sentence. Screenshots: `phone-pupil-2-1-start.png`, `phone-pupil-2-1-twist.png`, `phone-pupil-2-1-judged.png`. Fix: remove the nonexistent example reference and ask explicitly whether both forms are grammatical with different meanings; if an intended model meaning is supplied, accept correcting the changed meaning.

Coverage evidence: `coverage.json` and `actions.jsonl`; command `python qa/playtest-codex/scene-pupil/play.py` exited 0. Completed all 18 scene and all 6 pupil rounds on each device, every session picker entry, wrong answers in each session, 18 mid-round reloads with unchanged UI text, no page errors. Used phone taps with 390×844 mobile/touch context and desktop clicks at 1440×900. Inspected all 176 main-run screenshots via full-resolution phone sheets and half-resolution desktop sheets; inspected finding screenshots individually. Fresh-context scene recheck command `python qa/playtest-codex/scene-pupil/recheck.py` exited 0; both settled screenshots inspected.
Not covered: physical phones/other engines, all permutations of teaching-card order or scene positions. No source edits, rebuilds, or server restarts.

