# Café and Family Threads play-test notes

Live target: http://localhost:3417. Headless installed Python Playwright, fresh Chromium contexts; phone 390×844 with mobile/touch and tap, desktop 1440×900 with click. No build, restart, source edit, dependency install, or system change. Browsers closed.

## Concrete findings, worst first

1. **P2 — Café loses the clarification after a wrong response.** `/play/cafe`, session 1 “Same words, new job”, round 1; both viewports. Choose “Bring her a fresh hot tea.”, then “Ask first: Shall I close the window?”. The Ask button disappears but the bubble still says “Thank you — but this one is still hot. It's the draught, really.”; the clarification answer is absent. Reload retains the same wrong-response bubble. Also reproduced in S1 R2 and S2 R1/R5. Screenshot: `qa/playtest-codex/cafe-family/cafe-phone-s1-r1-ask-after-wrong.png`; desktop counterpart `cafe-desktop-s1-r1-ask-after-wrong.png`; persistent state `cafe-phone-s1-r1-reloaded.png`. Fix: make Ask display its answer even when a wrong choice exists; preserve miss history separately from the displayed conversation turn.

2. **P2 — Café clarification question runs off the phone.** `/play/cafe`, session 2 “Which one?”, round 1, 390×844. Open session 2 and read the Ask button. Its single-line label runs beyond the right edge; “chocolate one?” is clipped in the viewport. Full-page width is 455 px; isolated reproduction after 500 ms reports document scrollWidth 455 with a configured 390 px viewport. Screenshot: `qa/playtest-codex/cafe-family/cafe-phone-s2-r1-viewport.png`; full-page `cafe-phone-s2-r1-prompt.png`; metrics in `play.jsonl` label `s2-r1-overflow-metrics`. Fix: wrap the Ask label with normal whitespace and allow automatic button height while retaining a minimum touch target.

3. **P3 — Family reload drops the pending card and repair feedback.** `/play/family`, session 1 “What is a game?”, round 4; both viewports. Choose chess, poker, then the wrong “are played with a ball” link; reload. Chess remains in the chain, but selected poker, all link choices, and the corrective feedback disappear. The learner must select poker again before continuing. Also reproduced S2 “What is a tool?” R4 with ruler → hammer → wrong cut link. Screenshots: `qa/playtest-codex/cafe-family/family-phone-s1-r4-wrong.png` and `family-phone-s1-r4-reloaded.png`; desktop counterparts exist. Fix: persist the pending card identifier and current repair feedback with the round draft, restoring them alongside the chain.

4. **P3 — Tool name is cut off in the newcomer row.** `/play/family`, session 2 “What is a tool?”, round 5, 390×844. Reach the nails round and inspect the six reference cards. “the screwdriver” is visibly cut off as “the screwdri…” without an ellipsis; the clipped part is hidden by the card. Screenshot: `qa/playtest-codex/cafe-family/family-phone-s2-r5-prompt.png`. Fix: use a phone layout with sufficient card width (such as two rows of three), or wrap long card words without clipping.

## Exact coverage

| Page | Session | Phone | Desktop |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Café | 1: Same words, new job | R1–R6 solved, end screen | R1–R6 solved, end screen |
| Café | 2: Which one? | R1–R6 solved, end screen | R1–R6 solved, end screen |
| Café | 3: Excuse me? | R1–R6 solved, end screen | R1–R6 solved, end screen |
| Family | 1: What is a game? | R1–R6 solved, end screen | R1–R6 solved, end screen |
| Family | 2: What is a tool? | R1–R5 solved, end screen | R1–R5 solved, end screen |

- Every round received a deliberate wrong answer, reload and successful correction; every live session picker entry was selected. Thread rounds also exercised taking back the last card and continuing. Newcomer rounds covered both “both” and “unlike”.
- End-screen evidence: `cafe-{phone,desktop}-s{1,2,3}-complete.png` and `family-{phone,desktop}-s{1,2}-complete.png` under this directory.
- `play.jsonl` contains visible UI text and before/after reload comparisons. Only Family thread R4 in each session changed its main text after reload; no captured page errors.
- 284 generated PNG screenshots are listed in `audit-manifest.json`. All were visually inspected in `audit-01.jpg` through `audit-24.jpg`; round prompts were additionally reviewed in ten `contact-*.jpg` sheets. Findings were inspected at full screenshot size.
- Commands used: `python qa/playtest-codex/cafe-family/play.py`, followed by `--family-only` to continue beyond lost pending-card input, then `python qa/playtest-codex/cafe-family/finish.py` to verify final tools completion. The intermediate tools assertion expected singular “joins” but live correct feedback says “nails join”; this was a script mismatch, not a product defect.
- Not covered: audible speech quality, physical device/browser behavior beyond emulated Chromium, every possible valid answer path. Live Family exposes two sessions; source-only extra sessions were not part of the running production UI.

